/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
Cargo.lock.bak
.lopi/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
lopi.toml
mutants.out/

# Scratch output from ad hoc/in-progress `cargo mutants` runs (Sprint P2 pre-flight
# PF-0/PF-3). mutants.out/ above already covers the raw per-mutant directory; this also
# excludes this directory's own top-level .log redirects. The committed artifact from a
# completed baseline run is a compact summary (kiban's `bench_results/<repo>/*.json`
# convention, see kiban's lib/bench.py), not this raw working directory.
/bench_results/

# E2E screenshots are delivered separately, not committed (binary blobs)
artifacts/screenshots/

# Locally-built plugin binary — see scripts/build-plugin-bin.sh. Not
# committed: platform-specific, and Track B (MCPB) is where prebuilt
# cross-platform binaries eventually come from.
/plugin/bin/

# Swift Package Manager build output (packages/LopiStacksKit) and
# packaged MCP bundles — build artifacts, not source.
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.mcpb

# cargo-fuzz build output and crash artifacts (Sprint S12, Phase 2) — the
# corpus under fuzz/corpus/ IS committed; these are not.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
